#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:1
msgid "Release 2.31.0 (2025-08-21)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:3
msgid ""
"`build-cores = 0` now auto-detects CPU cores [\\#13402](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/13402)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:5
msgid ""
"When `build-cores` is set to `0`, Nix now automatically detects the number "
"of available CPU cores and passes this value via `NIX_BUILD_CORES`, instead "
"of passing `0` directly. This matches the behavior when `build-cores` is "
"unset. This prevents the builder from having to detect the number of cores."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:7
msgid ""
"Fix Git LFS SSH issues [\\#13337](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/13337) "
"[\\#13743](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13743)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:9
msgid "Fixed some outstanding issues with Git LFS and SSH."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:11
msgid "Added support for `NIX_SSHOPTS`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:12
msgid "Properly use the parsed port from URL."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:13
msgid ""
"Better use of the response of `git-lfs-authenticate` to determine API "
"endpoint when the API is not exposed on port 443."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:15
msgid ""
"Add support for `user@address:port` syntax in store URIs [\\#7044](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/7044) [\\#3425](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/3425)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:17
msgid ""
"It's now possible to specify the port used for SSH stores directly in the "
"store URL in accordance with [RFC3986](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/"
"rfc3986). Previously the only way to specify custom ports was via "
"`ssh_config` or the `NIX_SSHOPTS` environment variable, because Nix "
"incorrectly passed the port number together with the host name to the SSH "
"executable."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:19
msgid ""
"This change affects [store references](../store/types/index.md#store-url-"
"format) passed via the `--store` and similar flags in CLI as well as in the "
"configuration for [remote builders](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-"
"builders). For example, the following store URIs now work:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:21
msgid "`ssh://127.0.0.1:2222`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:22
msgid "`ssh://[b573:6a48:e224:840b:6007:6275:f8f7:ebf3]:22`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:23
msgid "`ssh-ng://[b573:6a48:e224:840b:6007:6275:f8f7:ebf3]:22`"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:25
msgid ""
"Represent IPv6 RFC4007 ZoneId literals in conformance with RFC6874 [\\#13445]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13445)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:27
msgid ""
"Prior versions of Nix since [\\#4646](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/"
"4646) accepted [IPv6 scoped addresses](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/"
"rfc4007) in URIs like [store references](../store/types/index.md#store-url-"
"format) in the textual representation with a literal percent character: "
"`[fe80::1%18]`. This was ambiguous, because the the percent literal `%` is "
"reserved by [RFC3986](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc3986), since "
"it's used to indicate percent encoding. Nix now requires that the percent "
"`%` symbol is percent-encoded as `%25`. This implements [RFC6874](https://"
"datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc6874), which defines the representation of "
"zone identifiers in URIs. The example from above now has to be specified as "
"`[fe80::1%2518]`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:29
msgid ""
"Use WAL mode for SQLite cache databases [\\#13800](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/13800)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:31
msgid ""
"Previously, Nix used SQLite's \"truncate\" mode for caches. However, this "
"could cause a Nix process to block if another process was updating the "
"cache. This was a problem for the flake evaluation cache in particular, "
"since it uses long-running transactions. Thus, concurrent Nix commands "
"operating on the same flake could be blocked for an unbounded amount of "
"time. WAL mode avoids this problem."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:33
msgid ""
"This change required updating the versions of the SQLite caches. For "
"instance, `eval-cache-v5.sqlite` is now `eval-cache-v6.sqlite`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:35
msgid ""
"Enable parallel marking in bdwgc [\\#13708](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/13708)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:37
msgid ""
"Previously marking was done by only one thread, which takes a long time if "
"the heap gets big. Enabling parallel marking speeds up evaluation a lot, for "
"example (on a Ryzen 9 5900X 12-Core):"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:39
msgid "`nix search nixpkgs` from 24.3s to 18.9s."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:40
msgid ""
"Evaluating the `NixOS/nix/2.21.2` flake regression test from 86.1s to 71.2s."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:42
msgid ""
"New command `nix flake prefetch-inputs` [\\#13565](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/13565)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:44
msgid ""
"This command fetches all inputs of a flake in parallel. This can be a lot "
"faster than the serialized on-demand fetching during regular flake "
"evaluation. The downside is that it may fetch inputs that aren't normally "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:46
msgid ""
"Add `warn-short-path-literals` setting [\\#13489](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/13489)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:48
msgid ""
"This setting, when enabled, causes Nix to emit warnings when encountering "
"relative path literals that don't start with `.` or `/`, for instance "
"suggesting that `foo/bar` should be rewritten to `./foo/bar`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:50
msgid ""
"When updating a lock, respect the input's lock file [\\#13437](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/13437)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:52
msgid ""
"For example, if a flake has a lock for `a` and `a/b`, and we change the "
"flakeref for `a`, previously Nix would fetch the latest version of `b` "
"rather than using the lock for `b` from `a`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:54
msgid ""
"Implement support for Git hashing with SHA-256 [\\#13543](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/13543)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.31.md:56
msgid ""
"The experimental support for [Git-hashing](../development/experimental-"
"features.md#xp-feature-git-hashing) store objects now also includes support "
"for SHA-256, not just SHA-1, in line with upstream Git."
msgstr ""

